quran[23]{c,v,t}:
  26,184,And be conscious of Him Who created you and the earlier generations.’
  26,185,They said: ‘You are simply one of the bewitched.
  26,186,You are nothing but a human being like us. And we indeed consider you to be among the liars.
  26,187,So make pieces of the heaven fall upon us if you are among the truthful.’
  26,188,He (Shu‘ayb) said: ‘My Lord knows best what you are doing.’
  26,189,"So they rejected him, and then the punishment of the day of the shady cloud overtook them. No doubt, that was the punishment of a terrible day."
  26,190,"There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them are not believers."
  26,191,"And indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,192,"Indeed, this (Qur’an) is a revelation of the Lord of all worlds."
  26,193,"The Trustworthy Spirit (Gabriel) has descended with it,"
  26,194,upon your heart so that you may be among the warners.
  26,195,(It has been revealed) in a clear Arabic language.
  26,196,"Indeed, it is (foretold) in the scriptures of the ancients."
  26,197,Is it not enough proof for them that the learned men of the Children of Israel (already) recognise it?
  26,198,"Had We revealed it to some non-Arab,"
  26,199,"who would have recited it to them (in fluent Arabic), they would still not have believed in it."
  26,200,This is how We cause (denial) to pass through the hearts of the guilty.
  26,201,They will not believe in it until they see the painful punishment.
  26,202,"So, it will come upon them suddenly while they are unaware."
  26,203,Then they will say: ‘Shall we be granted respite?’
  26,204,Do they seek to hasten Our punishment?
  26,205,"Just think: if We let them enjoy (themselves) for some years,"
  26,206,"then (the torment) which they have been promised comes upon them,"
